prompt:
Implement a 3D particle fireworks system using Three.js.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Interaction and Lifecycle]
(1) Click the canvas's "sky" area (the upper half of the view) to launch one firework in that direction;
(2) Lifecycle of a single firework: ascent phase (one bright particle flies upward along the launch direction) → explosion (bursts at the explosion point with at least 200 particles distributed over a spherical surface) → falling fade-out (falls under gravity and is removed from the scene after its opacity reaches 0);
(3) For each explosion, randomly select a color from the palette: red, gold, green, blue, purple, white;
(4) Particles must use THREE.Points, with either a custom ShaderMaterial or a PointsMaterial with size attenuation;
(5) After the explosion, particles are affected by gravity, with a vertically downward acceleration of approximately 2.0 units/s² (correctly multiplied by the frame dt);
(6) The ascending projectile should preferably have a brief trailing streak/trail (optional to implement, but the prompt encourages implementing a fading trail);

[Buttons and Scene]
(7) Auto-launch button id="autoBtn": when enabled, automatically launch one firework in a random direction every 1–2 seconds;
(8) Clear-all button id="clearBtn": clear all particles/fireworks that have not yet disappeared;
(9) Use OrbitControls and a dark background;

[HUD]
(10) Display: current total number of active particles id="particleCount", cumulative number of explosions id="explosionCount", and frame rate id="fps";

[State Exposure (Required)]
(11) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame with: particleCount (number of active particles), explosionCount (cumulative number of explosions), activeFireworks (current number of unfinished fireworks/bursts, an integer), and simTime (simulation time in seconds). When auto-launch is enabled, it is recommended to additionally set autoFireworks: true for easier debugging (optional field; if implemented, it must remain consistent with the button state).

Output a single HTML file and open it through a local HTTP server.
